  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145722",
      "title": "Using \"getServerSideProps\" for Server-side Rendering",
      "lectureOrder": 282,
      "videoOrder": 263,
      "sourceHash": "696907a7a5320a171bbba1015f9ca417217e00025c3c502b5b13e9ab1a996b99",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.15,
          "end": 3.28,
          "en": "So let's say we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.28,
          "end": 8.28,
          "en": "a dummy user profile js file here in the pages folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.58,
          "end": 13.2,
          "en": "So a user profile page for which I'll add a component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.2,
          "end": 16.68,
          "en": "the UserProfilePage component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.68,
          "end": 20.64,
          "en": "And in here, we want to get some users specific data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.64,
          "end": 23.09,
          "en": "and show that on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.09,
          "end": 25.69,
          "en": "So of course we export that like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.69,
          "end": 29.9,
          "en": "but now that's a page, which we can't pre-render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.9,
          "end": 32.59,
          "en": "because we need to know for which user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.59,
          "end": 34.19,
          "en": "we are rendering this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.19,
          "end": 38.68,
          "en": "Now we could expect a user ID as part of the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.68,
          "end": 40.55,
          "en": "So we could make this kind of dynamic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.55,
          "end": 43.21,
          "en": "and expect to use the ID instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.21,
          "end": 47.07,
          "en": "But then everyone who enters this ID in the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.07,
          "end": 50.68,
          "en": "is able to see some data for that given user ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.68,
          "end": 52.83,
          "en": "So that's not what I want here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.83,
          "end": 56.91,
          "en": "Instead, we wanna identify the user making the request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.91,
          "end": 60.73,
          "en": "let's say with help of a cookie which we set before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.73,
          "end": 62.64,
          "en": "Now at the moment we don't have that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.64,
          "end": 65.19,
          "en": "We didn't add any authentication,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.19,
          "end": 68.92,
          "en": "we're not placing any cookies on the user's machine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.92,
          "end": 72.15,
          "en": "and therefore, we don't really have to use case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.15,
          "end": 75.94,
          "en": "but it hopefully is a scenario that's easy to imagine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.94,
          "end": 79.25,
          "en": "And the later in the course we'll dive into authentication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.25,
          "end": 82.64,
          "en": "and we'll then have this actual scenario.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.64,
          "end": 84.53999999999999,
          "en": "So therefore here, we wanna return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.53999999999999,
          "end": 86.5,
          "en": "some user specific data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.5,
          "end": 90.45,
          "en": "let's say to user name, but again, we need to get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.45,
          "end": 92.36,
          "en": "to the request object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.36,
          "end": 95.03,
          "en": "which carries the cookies and the headers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.03,
          "end": 99,
          "en": "to find out which users sent this request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99,
          "end": 102.43299999999999,
          "en": "That would be a typical use case for getServerSideProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.55,
          "end": 105.67,
          "en": "We can't pre-rendered as page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.67,
          "end": 109.17,
          "en": "because we don't know which users will have in advance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.17,
          "end": 112.3,
          "en": "and we don't get access to their cookies in advance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.318,
          "end": 116.7,
          "en": "Therefore, we want to export an async function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.7,
          "end": 119.797,
          "en": "an async function called getServerSideProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.57,
          "end": 124.78,
          "en": "Now, we get a context object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.78,
          "end": 127.35,
          "en": "at which we'll take a closer look in a second,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.35,
          "end": 130.26,
          "en": "and we also need to return an object here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.26,
          "end": 132.43,
          "en": "and the object which be returned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.43,
          "end": 135.71,
          "en": "actually needs to have the same format",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.71,
          "end": 138.45,
          "en": "as it does in getStaticProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.45,
          "end": 141.84,
          "en": "So that return object does not change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.84,
          "end": 143.71,
          "en": "It should have a props key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.71,
          "end": 146.07,
          "en": "it can have a not found key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.07,
          "end": 148.98,
          "en": "and it can have a redirect key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.98,
          "end": 151.95,
          "en": "The only difference is the revalidate key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.95,
          "end": 156.2,
          "en": "That is not required here and the debts can't be set here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.2,
          "end": 159.94,
          "en": "because getStaticProps per definition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 159.94,
          "end": 162.63,
          "en": "runs for every incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 162.63,
          "end": 165.091,
          "en": "So there's no need to revalidate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 165.091,
          "end": 167.03,
          "en": "after a certain amount of seconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 167.03,
          "end": 169.893,
          "en": "because it will always run again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 170.94,
          "end": 174.54,
          "en": "So therefore we return an object with props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 174.54,
          "end": 175.82999999999998,
          "en": "which makes sense Since, I guess,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 175.82999999999998,
          "end": 178.577,
          "en": "since it's called getServerSideProps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 179.69,
          "end": 180.523,
          "en": "and these props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 180.523,
          "end": 182.69,
          "en": "will then be made available to this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 182.69,
          "end": 186.25,
          "en": "which will still be called by Next.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 186.25,
          "end": 187.65,
          "en": "But as mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 187.65,
          "end": 191.57,
          "en": "it will not be called in advance when we built the project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 191.57,
          "end": 194.203,
          "en": "but really for every incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 195.21,
          "end": 198.5,
          "en": "So here we could then have a username prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 198.5,
          "end": 201.77,
          "en": "which I afforded moment hard code to Max.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 201.77,
          "end": 205.46,
          "en": "And then here we output prop props.username",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 205.46,
          "end": 206.973,
          "en": "in the component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 208.4,
          "end": 210.66,
          "en": "And if we do all of that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 210.66,
          "end": 214.94,
          "en": "and we then visit slash user profile page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 214.94,
          "end": 217.2,
          "en": "so this page which we just added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.2,
          "end": 219.82999999999998,
          "en": "we see Max here at the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 219.82999999999998,
          "end": 221.81,
          "en": "So that works and that proofs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 221.81,
          "end": 223.9,
          "en": "that getsServerSideProps works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 223.9,
          "end": 227.37,
          "en": "because that's where the value Max is coming from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 227.37,
          "end": 230.05,
          "en": "But the important thing now really is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 230.05,
          "end": 235.05,
          "en": "that this only executes on the server after deployment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 235.48,
          "end": 237.99,
          "en": "and also on our development server here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 237.99,
          "end": 240.96,
          "en": "but it's not statically pre-generated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 240.96,
          "end": 243.573,
          "en": "And that has a couple of important implications.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
